# ===========================================================================
#  Mistari ya mwisho (line endings) — na kwa nini inahusu USHAHIDI
#
#  Sahihi za PD zinafunga SHA256 ya faili la ushahidi. Git ikibadilisha CRLF
#  kuwa LF wakati wa commit, bytes zilizohifadhiwa si zile zilizohashiwa, na
#  `verify` inasema "ushahidi umebadilika baada ya kusainiwa" kwa faili
#  ambalo hakuna aliyeligusa.
#
#  Halikuwa tatizo pale `research/reports/` haikuwa ikipushwa. Reports
#  zilipoanza kusafiri na repo (2026-08-14), likawa tatizo mara moja.
#
#  `-text` inamaanisha: git isiguse mistari ya faili hizi hata kidogo.
# ===========================================================================

research/reports/** -text
*.json                -text

# HALI ILIYOPO (2026-08-14): sahihi #1–#19 zilihashi faili zilizoandikwa kwa
# CRLF kwenye Windows, kabla ya `newline="\n"` kuwekwa kwenye waandishi. Faili
# hizo zilipocommitiwa, git ilizigeuza LF. Kwa hiyo:
#   · kwenye mashine ya PD  → zinabaki CRLF, `verify` inapita
#   · kwenye clone mpya      → zitakuwa LF, hash hazitalingana
# Sio kasoro inayohitaji kurekebishwa leo: mrithi (supersession) unashughulikia,
# na ripoti zinazoandikwa kuanzia sasa ni LF kila mahali. Lakini isije
# ikashangaza mtu — imeandikwa hapa.

# Scripts za Windows zinahitaji CRLF ili `cmd` iziendeshe kwa uhakika.
*.bat text eol=crlf
